What does this method check for a 2D array `grid`?

```java
public boolean containsValue(int[][] grid, int target) {
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            if (grid[r][c] == target) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```

What does this method compute for `grid = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}`?

```java
public int[] rowSums(int[][] grid) {
    int[] sums = new int[grid.length];
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        int rowSum = 0;
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            rowSum += grid[r][c];
        }
        sums[r] = rowSum;
    }
    return sums;
}
```

What does this method compute for `grid = {{5, 1}, {3, 8}, {2, 9}}`?

```java
public int findMax(int[][] grid) {
    int max = grid[0][0];
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            if (grid[r][c] > max) {
                max = grid[r][c];
            }
        }
    }
    return max;
}
```

